paras.en:
“Alight, travellers! The journey is complete;
there will be no more marching till the Resurrection; the abode is here.
This land is the place of slaughter, this the shrine of the Imam;
unload the camels and set up the tents.
Spread beds with eagerness on this holy ground;
the water of immortality has been sprinkled on the dust here.”

“This is the provision of the travellers and this the stock;
this dust is higher in rank than the water of Khizr.
The good-natured man who casts it into the storm,
the favourable wind will bring him the pearl of desire.
In despair he will see the mercy of the Disposer of affairs;
the river will hold the ship with the hand of the wave.”

Saying this, the captain of the ship of the Ummah alighted;
all who were mounted became footsore on foot.
The Imam smilingly said to each one:
“See! What a meadow, what a stream, what an atmosphere!”
Akbar blossomed on seeing the desert;
Abbas began to sway on seeing the river.
